#hasheq((content-digest . "5079f879eddee5bf8798ca98face26d13ab179e5abd7bca97a2d58504ef73104") (milestone . 896) (plan-id . "fb67e0429ed155a4b4e3f31afe3ef3ca7748ee891c06247b11e5e2a86cfebd75") (report . "Eighteen independent review rounds against the frozen W5 wave doc, ending with R18 APPROVED at this exact head. R1 found three defects (nested provenance fields disabled by non-matching ancestor keys; the F13 restore could not restore a stale PLAN.md; a legacy manifest hash broken by a trailing empty element). R2 refused a non-reproducible matrix recorded head (the generator now reads the pinned observation from the committed matrix so regeneration is byte-identical). R3 refused an unbound tree/digest gap; R4 refused a non-canonical current-wave SHA256SUMS. R5 refused timing values from unrelated numeric fields and an uncaught exception on malformed SUMS lines. R6/R7 refused non-recursive JSON coverage. R8 refused the missing F7 register guard, unverified recorded sha256 fields, and the intra-JSON-only cross-artifact check. R9 refused tree fields walked as commits, a subtractive timing set, and non-Python-compatible canonical escapes. R10 refused an order-dependent report scan and one-level artifact discovery. R11 refused branch-dependent gate strictness and a crash on directory-relative current-wave SUMS entries. R12 refused discovery that did not implement the documented artifacts/**/v*/ scope. R13 required exact head binding for head-claiming fields while keeping ancestor semantics for pinned observation heads. R14 found no blocking defect. R15 refused the shallow-checkout skip that left CI green without exercising the real tree (the workflows shard now checks out with fetch-depth 0) and the fail-open constrained path. R16 refused JSON null canonicalized as a quoted string. R17 refused a declared current wave that could pass with no artifact directory. R18 verified the whole wave at the final head and found no blocking defect. Every accepted item is documented in docs/reports/ARTIFACT-PROVENANCE-v1.00.31.md; the lint reports 941 historical provenance notes and zero drift at this head.") (reviewed-sha . "280835b3a3c9a56fe2a50ad7f194025614857d60") (reviewer . "pi-reviewer-subagent:readonly-w5-impl-review-r18:campaign-v1.00.31-w5-4a19d60b4:2026-09-23") (schema-version . 2) (scope . "W5 artifact provenance and determinism: scripts/ci/verify-artifact-provenance.rkt (SHA256SUMS binding with recursive coverage and both historical spellings plus typed refusal for a directory-relative current entry, provenance heads with exact binding for head-claiming fields and ancestor semantics for pinned observation heads, paired tree validation, canonical JSON byte-compatible with Python json.dumps(ensure_ascii=True) including the JSON null symbol, cross-artifact prose/structured timing agreement across bound markdown reports against the complete per-version timing union, recorded-digest-to-file verification, recursive discovery over artifacts/**/v*, and a declared current wave that must exist), the coordinator artifact-provenance gate with branch-independent current-wave derivation (extensions/gsd/delivery-coordinator.rkt), the F7 register guard (tests/test-wave-delivery-integrity-register.rkt), the CI workflow shard's full-history checkout (.github/workflows/ci.yml), tests/test-artifact-provenance.rkt (26 tests), the deterministic generator and bound artifacts under artifacts/wave-delivery-integrity/v1.00.31-w5/, docs/reports/ARTIFACT-PROVENANCE-v1.00.31.md, and the F13 frozen-contract staleness guard in extensions/gsd/{plan-snapshot,campaign-state,campaign-repository}.rkt at implementation head 280835b3a3c9a56fe2a50ad7f194025614857d60 with content digest 5079f879eddee5bf8798ca98face26d13ab179e5abd7bca97a2d58504ef73104.") (timestamp . "2026-09-23T00:00:00Z") (verdict . "APPROVED") (wave . "W5"))
